1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:01,394
Before a surgeon operates on a real person,

2
00:00:01,413 --> 00:00:02,928
they need hundreds of hours of hands-on practice.

3
00:00:02,928 --> 00:00:05,064
That practice happens in simulation labs that

4
00:00:05,064 --> 00:00:06,982
cost hundreds of thousands of dollars and most

5
00:00:06,982 --> 00:00:07,992
students never get near one.

6
00:00:07,992 --> 00:00:09,590
We wanted to know how much of that training

7
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:10,549
could reach anyone with a laptop.

8
00:00:10,549 --> 00:00:11,879
So we started with questions.

9
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:14,366
How are surgeons actually trained and tested?

10
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:17,061
We found FLS, the keyhole-skills exam surgeons

11
00:00:17,061 --> 00:00:19,029
must pass to become board-certified, and OSATS,

12
00:00:19,029 --> 00:00:20,712
which grades five things.

13
00:00:20,712 --> 00:00:22,899
Respect for tissue, time and motion, instrument

14
00:00:22,899 --> 00:00:23,993
handling, flow and precision.

15
00:00:23,993 --> 00:00:26,214
Then we asked what makes these skills hard.

16
00:00:26,214 --> 00:00:28,182
The answer was tremor and the fulcrum effect.

17
00:00:28,182 --> 00:00:31,211
In keyhole surgery, the tool pivots at the skin.

18
00:00:31,211 --> 00:00:33,698
So your hand goes left and the tip goes right.

19
00:00:33,735 --> 00:00:35,179
Those became our core mechanics.

20
00:00:35,299 --> 00:00:37,722
We compared the alternatives, cadavers, box

21
00:00:37,722 --> 00:00:39,489
trainers, and VR simulators, and every one of

22
00:00:39,489 --> 00:00:40,717
them needs money or hardware.

23
00:00:40,717 --> 00:00:41,758
A browser doesn't.

24
00:00:41,945 --> 00:00:43,754
Steady Hands has three drills and five real

25
00:00:43,754 --> 00:00:44,477
procedures.

26
00:00:44,477 --> 00:00:46,597
The drills isolate one skill each, cutting at

27
00:00:46,597 --> 00:00:50,299
the right depth, placing sutures, and peg transfer.

28
00:00:50,299 --> 00:00:52,772
The actual FLS task, the procedures combine

29
00:00:52,772 --> 00:00:54,825
them in appendectomy.

30
00:00:54,825 --> 00:00:57,988
You find the appendix without nicking its artery.

31
00:00:57,988 --> 00:01:00,747
While the patient's heart reacts to every careless

32
00:01:00,747 --> 00:01:03,473
move, a central line is guided by live ultrasound.

33
00:01:03,473 --> 00:01:05,927
The vein squashes under the probe, the artery

34
00:01:06,064 --> 00:01:06,216
pulses.

35
00:01:06,216 --> 00:01:08,958
In a gallbladder removal, you must prove the

36
00:01:08,958 --> 00:01:11,902
critical view of safety before clipping.

37
00:01:11,902 --> 00:01:14,578
And if you pick the bile duct, the game stops

38
00:01:14,578 --> 00:01:16,799
you the way a senior surgeon would.

39
00:01:16,799 --> 00:01:20,147
Every run ends with an OSATS-style report and

40
00:01:20,147 --> 00:01:23,949
a sourced fact, and a trivia mode teaches the

41
00:01:23,949 --> 00:01:24,185
why.

42
00:01:24,185 --> 00:01:26,675
That means combining surgery, anatomy, physiology,

43
00:01:26,675 --> 00:01:28,660
ultrasound physics, and medical education research,

44
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,309
then turning them into game design.

45
00:01:30,309 --> 00:01:34,196
It's built in three.js, and every organ, instrument,

46
00:01:34,196 --> 00:01:36,518
and drape is generated in code.

47
00:01:36,518 --> 00:01:38,587
No downloaded models and no gore.

48
00:01:38,587 --> 00:01:41,330
So it loads in seconds and even on a school

49
00:01:41,330 --> 00:01:41,464
Chromebook.

50
00:01:41,464 --> 00:01:45,401
Ten times more, players, costs nothing because

51
00:01:45,401 --> 00:01:47,034
it's just static files.

52
00:01:47,034 --> 00:01:50,180
Ten times bigger means VR, haptic controllers,

53
00:01:50,180 --> 00:01:52,569
and instructor dashboard for a whole class.

54
00:01:52,569 --> 00:01:53,107
Plenty broke.

55
00:01:53,107 --> 00:01:56,523
Our first project, a wildfire predictor, didn't

56
00:01:56,523 --> 00:01:59,787
fit any track, so we pivoted mid-event.

57
00:01:59,787 --> 00:02:03,303
Our first art looked cartoonish, so we rebuilt

58
00:02:03,303 --> 00:02:05,222
it for grounded realism.

59
00:02:05,222 --> 00:02:07,880
To test fairly, we built automatic first-time

60
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:11,108
players that moved a real mouse with shaky hands.

61
00:02:11,346 --> 00:02:14,358
They found a drill that dropped to one frame

62
00:02:14,358 --> 00:02:17,639
per second and a step that could soft-lock.

63
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:21,592
We fixed both and re-ran until every level could

64
00:02:21,592 --> 00:02:22,400
be finished.

65
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,763
Then we showed it to Dr.

66
00:02:23,763 --> 00:02:26,034
Enver Ozer, a head and neck surgeon and professor

67
00:02:26,034 --> 00:02:27,162
at Ohio State.

68
00:02:27,162 --> 00:02:29,113
He said that suturing and trivia are the most

69
00:02:29,113 --> 00:02:29,450
valuable parts.

70
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:31,570
Because incisions are a skill he mostly acquired

71
00:02:31,570 --> 00:02:33,168
from real experience, he suggested injections,

72
00:02:33,168 --> 00:02:35,658
more types of suturing, and more procedures.

73
00:02:35,658 --> 00:02:37,086
So that's our roadmap.

74
00:02:37,274 --> 00:02:39,394
Injection training and new suturing techniques

75
00:02:39,394 --> 00:02:40,067
come next.

76
00:02:40,067 --> 00:02:41,831
Ahead of new incision drills.

77
00:02:42,035 --> 00:02:44,492
Steady hands is for pre-med students, med school

78
00:02:44,492 --> 00:02:46,696
applicants, and schools or hospitals without

79
00:02:46,696 --> 00:02:47,419
a sim lab.

80
00:02:47,419 --> 00:02:50,529
We'll test it with students and residents to

81
00:02:50,751 --> 00:02:52,736
check that the scores really help separate beginners

82
00:02:52,736 --> 00:02:53,123
from experts.

83
00:02:53,123 --> 00:02:55,579
The same way the FLS exam was validated.
